# DEPRECATED: Git-Crypt Guide

**⚠️ This guide is DEPRECATED. This repository has migrated to SOPS.**

**See:** [SOPS_GUIDE.md](SOPS_GUIDE.md) for current encryption documentation.

---

## Why We Migrated

Git-crypt provides file-level encryption only - entire files are encrypted as binary blobs. This made configuration files unreadable on GitHub, defeating the purpose of version control for infrastructure-as-code.

SOPS provides **partial encryption** - only sensitive values (API keys, passwords, tokens) are encrypted while the file structure remains readable. This gives us:

✅ Readable configs on GitHub
✅ Meaningful git diffs
✅ Better code review
✅ Easier troubleshooting
✅ True infrastructure-as-code

## Migration Completed

All files previously encrypted with git-crypt have been migrated to SOPS:

-  - Configarr API keys
-  - Overseerr config (partial encryption)
-  - Bazarr config (partial encryption)
-  - Homarr config (partial encryption)
-  - Prowlarr config (partial encryption)
-  - Cloudflare credentials

The git-crypt encryption key can be safely discarded as it is no longer used.

